[2026-11-20T14:33:37.024Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"gh pr view 103 --repo link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer --json title,body,url --jq '.body' | head -120 && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"Fixes #102\n\nThe merged Dependabot updates exposed stale workflow assertions, formatter changes and incomplete local-package lock metadata. This PR repairs those failures while preserving the upgrades, then refreshes the full npm, Deno, Python, Actions, toolchain and container dependency trees.\n\n- Regenerate all three npm locks and the frozen Deno graph; add a complete hash-locked Python benchmark graph. Synchronize active version pins and retain the patch Changeset for automated release.\n- Use current Node 26.13.0/npm 12.2.2, Bun 1.4.4, Deno 2.9.8 and exact current Action releases. Install npm before setup-node cache discovery. Lock the preview browser tools and match their Playwright container digest.\n- Replace handwritten semantic-version comparison and Windows command wrappers with `semver` and `cmd-shim`. Delegate BuildKit pull retries to the current upstream Action while preserving registry fallback, opt-out and tracing.\n- Derive benchmark scanner expectations from requirements, and exercise the actual hash-verified spaCy model and offline scanners in security CI. Keep artifact authentication/digests, extraction compatibility, cleanup callbacks and release behavior.\n\nThe [implementation comparison](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/compare/15f86c08069a53c65020fdb760512aac37929976...f52f39156884a6d10882e28c9b898a1b21b417a3) contains the 63 code/configuration changes before the raw evidence publication. The final publication also clarifies the contributor documentation.\n\n### Dependency evidence and compatibility limits\n\n[Evidence index](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/blob/issue-102-b6ecf86c9f05/dev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/README.md), [requirement mapping](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/blob/issue-102-b6ecf86c9f05/dev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/PLAN.md), [root-cause/migration analysis](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/blob/issue-102-b6ecf86c9f05/dev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/ANALYSIS.md) and [complete dependency tables](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/tree/issue-102-b6ecf86c9f05/dev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/dependencies) record every old/latest/resolved entry, source and retained constraint. These include transitive packages, removed/hoisted entries, inline tools, images and all 67 external Action references.\n\nPython 3.14.10 is the latest compatible security release: current Presidio caps preshed below the release that fixes Python 3.15 model loading. An actual CI reproduction fails with `OverflowError`; the same scanner test passes on 3.14.10. Temurin 21.0.13+9 remains the latest supported Java 21 patch for Capacitor's current Gradle template; Java 27 requires an unsupported template/toolchain migration. Other retained transitive versions name their upstream consumer constraints individually. All audited dependency graphs have zero reported vulnerabilities.\n\n### Reproduction and verification\n\nOn baseline main `15f86c0`, the Checks workflow fails Prettier at three loop statements, Workflows rejects its upgraded zizmor pair, and Example app installation rejects missing local rimraf metadata. Preserved complete logs and exact error lines are linked from [VALIDATION.md](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/blob/issue-102-b6ecf86c9f05/dev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/VALIDATION.md).\n\nRegression coverage includes `tests/ci-workflow-policy.test.js`, `tests/workflows-lint.test.js`, `tests/pipeline-requirements.test.js`, `tests/temp-cleanup.test.js`, `tests/changeset-config.test.js`, `tests/node-toolchain.test.js`, `tests/setup-npm.test.js` and the Python version/audit tests. CI also runs the real upstream Buildx Action/daemon with bounded recovered/exhausted pull faults and the actual NLP scanner smoke. No failing tests were skipped.\n\nLocal focused regressions, ESLint, Prettier, Ruff, actionlint, ShellCheck, zizmor, Vite production build, artifact archive roundtrip and desktop compatibility probes pass. The archive/desktop probes make deprecations fatal. All three npm audits, the complete 69-package Python audit and development-tool audit report zero findings. Full Node/Bun/Deno and Linux/Windows/macOS coverage runs on existing CI to respect the local memory limit; [live PR checks](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/pull/103/checks) identify the current commit. Optional Android/iOS dispatch jobs retain their existing opt-in policy and are not represented as successful PR builds.\n\n### Upstream reports\n\nExisting upstream discussions were searched before reporting; exact report bodies and returned URLs are saved under the evidence folder.\n\n| Dependency / retained integration | Report |\n| --- | --- |\n| temp legacy cleanup | [node-temp 100](https://github.com/bruce/node-temp/issues/100#issuecomment-6672682111) |\n| Artifact unzip Buffer deprecation | [toolkit 2003](https://github.com/actions/toolkit/issues/2003#issuecomment-6672682500) |\n| actionlint job self-reference | [actionlint 711](https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/issues/711#issuecomment-6672682896) |\n| actionlint concurrency queue schema | [actionlint 657](https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/issues/657#issuecomment-6672683280) |\n| setup-node/npm cache ordering | [setup-node 1553](https://github.com/actions/setup-node/issues/1553#issuecomment-6672683784) |\n| PyYAML Python 3.15 wheel availability | [PyYAML 951](https://github.com/yaml/pyyaml/issues/951#issuecomment-6672684219) |\n| Buildx registry failover | [setup-buildx 490](https://github.com/docker/setup-buildx-action/pull/490#issuecomment-6672972223) |\n| Artifact finalization retry/r