[2026-11-20T14:37:29.163Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_87","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"gh release view v4.39.4 --repo github/codeql-action --json body,url --jq .body | head -50 && gh release view v2.105.0 --repo cli/cli --json body,url --jq .body | head -85 && sed -n '1,115p' scripts/setup-preview-gh.sh\"","aggregated_output":"- Update default CodeQL bundle version to [2.27.5](https://github.com/github/codeql-action/releases/tag/codeql-bundle-v2.27.5). [#4333](https://github.com/github/codeql-action/pull/4333)\n## What's Changed\r\n\r\n## Subscribe to GitHub Event Streams with `gh event` (preview)\r\n\r\nThe new `gh event` command set lets agents, integrations, and scripts wait for pull request changes instead of polling GitHub:\r\n\r\n```shell\r\n# Wait for a review event\r\ngh event listen --resource https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/pull/NUMBER --event com.github.pull_request.review.submitted.v1 --timeout 30m\r\n\r\n# Wait for a check suite completion event\r\ngh event listen --resource https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/pull/NUMBER --event com.github.pull_request.check_suite.status.changed.v1 --jq .data.conclusion\r\n\r\n# List active event subscriptions\r\ngh event subscription list\r\n```\r\n\r\nBy default, `gh event listen` exits after the first event. Use `--count` to wait for several events or `--follow` to keep listening. Events are printed as CloudEvent JSON objects, with `data.api_url` pointing to the resource that changed.\r\n\r\nSupported events include submitted reviews, pull request state and head changes, merge conflicts, and completed check suites. The `subscription create`, `list`, `view`, and `delete` commands manage subscriptions directly.\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> GitHub Event Streams is in preview. [Join the wait list](https://gh.io/event-streams-signup), read the [announcement](https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-github-event-streams-is-now-in-preview), or see the [Event Streams documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/integrations/how-tos/using-github-event-streams).\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n\r\n### ✨ Features\r\n\r\n* Add a server-sent events reader and Event Subscriptions API client by @babakks in [#15071](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15071)\r\n* Add `gh event listen` to wait for pull request events without polling by @babakks in [#15072](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15072)\r\n* Add `gh event subscription list` by @babakks in [#15073](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15073)\r\n* Add `gh event subscription create` by @babakks in [#15074](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15074)\r\n* Add `gh event subscription view` by @babakks in [#15075](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15075)\r\n* Add `gh event subscription delete` by @babakks in [#15076](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15076)\r\n* Suggest `gh event listen` to agents using `gh pr` and `gh api` by @babakks in [#15077](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15077)\r\n* Support check suite events and suggest them from `gh run view` and `gh run watch` by @babakks in [#15081](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15081)\r\n\r\n### 🐛 Fixes\r\n\r\n* fix(event listen): print each event without waiting for the next heartbeat by @babakks and @iancanderson in [#15079](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15079)\r\n* fix(event listen): report deleted subscriptions clearly by @babakks in [#15080](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15080)\r\n* fix(event): improve stream framing, `Retry-After` handling, evals, and regression coverage by @babakks in [#15083](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15083)\r\n\r\n### 📚 Docs & Chores\r\n\r\n* Make issue-triage formatting checks nonblocking by @BagToad in [#15052](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15052)\r\n* Add event-driven agent evals, `gh` skill guidance, and preview documentation by @babakks in [#15078](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15078)\r\n\r\n### :dependabot: Dependencies\r\n\r\n* chore(deps): bump `golang.org/x/text` from 0.43.0 to 0.44.0 by @dependabot in [#15049](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15049)\r\n* chore(deps): bump `golang.org/x/term` from 0.47.0 to 0.48.0 by @dependabot in [#15048](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15048)\r\n* chore(deps): bump `golang.org/x/crypto` from 0.58.0 to 0.59.0 by @dependabot in [#15064](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15064)\r\n* chore(deps): bump `zod` from 4.3.6 to 4.6.6 in `evals` by @dependabot in [#15086](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15086)\r\n* chore(deps): bump `@hono/node-server` from 2.1.5 to 2.1.9 in `evals` by @dependabot in [#15085](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15085)\r\n* chore(deps): bump `hono` from 4.13.13 to 4.13.19 in `evals` by @dependabot in [#15084](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15084)\r\n\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/cli/cli/compare/v2.104.0...v2.105.0\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Install the reviewed GitHub CLI inside the Linux x64 Playwright container.\n# GitHub-hosted runner utilities are not inherited by container jobs.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n: \"${RUNNER_TEMP:?RUNNER_TEMP is required}\"\n: \"${GITHUB_PATH:?GITHUB_PATH is required}\"\nif [[ \"$(uname -s)/$(uname -m)\" != Linux/x86_64 ]]; then\n  echo '::error::Preview GitHub CLI setup requires Linux x86_64.'\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nversion=2.103.3\nchecksum=4c806978ffce1cec70853302a56d70ac6da4f19bae7adca4e1a8ab00633dd91d\ninstall_dir=\"$(mktemp -d \"$RUNNER_TEMP/preview-gh.XXXXXX\")\"\narchive=\"$install_dir/gh.tar.gz\"\ntrap 'rm -f \"$archive\"' EXIT\n\n# Bound each attempt so a stalled transfer retries instead of hanging. No\n# retry starts after 50s and an attempt lasts at most 20s, so the download\n# ends within 70s, inside the step's 90s budget.\ncurl --fail --silent --show-error --location --retry 3 \\\n  --connect-timeout 15 --max-time 20 --retry-max-time 50 \\\n  \"https://github.com/cli/cli/releases/download/v${version}/gh_${version}_linux_amd64.tar.gz\" \\\n  --output \"$archive\"\nif ! printf '%s  %s\\n' \"$checksum\" \"$archive\" | sha256sum --check --status; then\n  echo '::error::Preview GitHub CLI archive checksum mismatch.' >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\ntar -xzf \"$archive\" -C \"$install_dir\" --strip-components=2 \\\n  \"gh_${version}_linux_amd64/bin/gh\"\n\"$install_dir/gh\" --version\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$install_dir\" >> \"$GITHUB_PATH\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
