grade to node 24 @salmanmkc (#186)\\r\\n- Upgrade IA Publish @Jcambass (#165)\\r\\n- Add workflow file for publish\ndev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/research/code-review.diff:2118: # Check maintained helpers without rewriting immutable downloaded evidence.\ndev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/research/trufflehog-latest.json:1:{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/releases/431835415\",\"assets_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/trufflesecurity/truf\ndev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/research/java21-latest.json:1:{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/adoptium/temurin21-binaries/releases/420500038\",\"assets_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/adoptium/temurin21-bina\ndev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/research/deploy-pages-latest.json:1:{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/actions/deploy-pages/releases/370458049\",\"assets_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/actions/deploy-pages/rel\ndev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/research/buildx-latest.json:1:{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/docker/buildx/releases/432835827\",\"assets_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/docker/buildx/releases/432835827/asse\ndev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/research/codeql-action-latest.json:1:{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/github/codeql-action/releases/434191629\",\"assets_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/github/codeql-action/re\ndev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/research/browser-commander-comparison.json:1:{\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/browser-commander/compare/v0.8.1...v0.34.1\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/link-fou\n# Issue 223 dependency refresh\n\nThe starting point is main commit `5c2804cf476e3eb4aed7ac09e2245e2617b447ab`. Dependabot PRs #212 and #222 were already merged. Issue 223 had one follow-up with the baseline CI results and no registered sub-issues. PR 224 initially contained only a draft placeholder and had no conversation comments, review comments or reviews.\n\n[Issue and follow-up](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/issues/223) · [Pull request](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/pull/224) · [Previous dependency refresh](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/pull/103)\n\n## Requirements and plan\n\n| Requirement | Options and implementation plan | Verification |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Repair errors caused by the already-merged Dependabot updates | Compare failed and succeeding runs on main to isolate persistent regressions. Reproduce the formatter failure with the version in the baseline lock, then apply its output. Keep the merged upgrades. | Baseline log lines, formatter before and after, audit results and the PR check suite. |\n| Update every JavaScript and TypeScript dependency, including dev tools and transitives | Compare the registry latest dist-tag with all active manifests, overrides, npm lock entries and Deno lock entries. Use the native npm resolver after adjusting direct constraints. Resolve Deno's graph separately with its own tool. Review consumer ranges before imposing a transitive major. | Three clean npm installs, frozen Deno graph, lock inventories, lint, Node/Bun/Deno tests and the example build. |\n| Update Python, the benchmark model and every Python tool | Compare with PyPI and model releases. Resolve the benchmark graph with uv and regenerate hashes for the tested Python version. Keep the previously captured Python requirements file as immutable evidence and review its pins in the dependency inventory. | Ruff, hash-locked scanner smoke and pip-audit on both active and captured requirements. |\n| Update all external workflow and composite references, toolchains, images and inline tools | Resolve Action releases and the commit behind each SHA pin, preserve pinning style, and keep versions synchronized where repeated. Compare image manifests with registry digests. | Actionlint, zizmor, ShellCheck, native build jobs and cross-runtime release checks. |\n| Keep Dependabot coverage complete | Keep grouped npm, pip and GitHub Actions updates. Add coverage for any missing active manifest or for a named historical directory if the issue explicitly requires it. | Compare directory coverage with the actual manifests and the GitHub documentation. |\n| Review major migrations and use upstream functionality | Review primary release notes and actual call sites. Remove a workaround when an upstream release supplies equivalent behavior, and verify callers through the existing entry point. | Migration notes with links and focused regression checks. |\n| Report remaining reusable logic, gaps and defects upstream | Review prior reports from PR 103 and search for duplicates before creating or updating a report. Include a reproducer, versions, workaround and proposed change for confirmed cases. | Upstream report URLs and affected integration notes in PR 224. |\n| Record every old, latest and selected version, with a reason for each exception | Query the registries before editing and reconcile the resulting npm, Deno, PyPI, Action and toolchain inventories against the final graph. | Dependency tables and compatibility evidence in this folder. |\n| Ship one tested PR with a normal release trigger | Add a patch changeset, merge any new main commits into the prepared branch, update PR 224 with a closing keyword and verify checks against the final head SHA. | Clean working tree, actual PR diff, CI results and the release guard. |\n\n## Existing components\n\n- npm's native resolver and registry audit work against a committed lockfile. npm-check-updates can discover new direct majors. Registry dist-tags still need to be compared with the locks for transitive packages. [npm audit and lockfile behavior](https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/audit/) · [npm-check-updates](https://github.com/raineorshine/npm-check-updates)\n- Deno's supported reproducible workflow is `deno ci`. `deno install --frozen=false` updates the graph before CI verifies it. [Deno dependency management](https://docs.deno.com/runtime/packages/)\n- uv compiles a complete, hash-pinned requirements file without installing the NLP stack to discover versions. pip-audit can audit that resolved graph. [uv requirements compilation](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/pip/compile/) · [pip-audit](https://github.com/pypa/pip-audit)\n- Dependabot already manages grouped updates in this repository. Renovate also supports package managers and inline dependency extraction when an upstream ecosystem has no native manifest. [Dependabot options](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/dependabot/working-with-dependabot/dependabot-options-reference) · [Renovate custom managers](https://docs.renovatebot.com/modules/manager/regex/)\n.github/workflows/release.yml:178:  version-check:\n.github/workflows/release.yml:205:  changeset-check:\n.github/workflows/release.yml:250:  lint:\n.github/workflows/release.yml:293:        run: npm run check:secrets\n.github/workflows/release.yml:308:        run: npm run lint:all -- --max-warnings 0\n.github/workflows/release.yml:314:        run: npm run check:duplication\n.github/workflows/release.yml:551:          tags: pr-check:${{ github.sha }}\npackage.json:71:    \"lint:all\": \"eslint .\",\npackage.json:72:    \"lint:fix\": \"eslint . --fix\",\npackage.json:75:    \"check:duplication\": \"jscpd .\",\npackage.json:76:    \"check:secrets\": \"[REDACTED]\\\"**/*\\\" && node scripts/check-secrets.mjs\",\npackage.json:77:    \"check\": \"npm run lint && npm run format:check && npm run check:duplication\",\n{\n  \"packageJson\": {\n    \"dependencies\": [\n      \"npm:@changesets/cli@^3.0.3\",\n      \"npm:@eslint/js@^10.0.1\",\n      \"npm:@faker-js/faker@^10.6.0\",\n      \"npm:@nlpjs/ner@4.27.0\",\n      \"npm:@secretlint/core@14.0.1\",\n      \"npm:@secretlint/profiler@14.0.1\",\n      \"npm:browser-commander@0.35.0\",\n      \"npm:cmd-shim@^9.0.2\",\n      \"npm:command-stream@3.0.0\",\n      \"npm:eslint-config-prettier@^10.1.8\",\n      \"npm:eslint-plugin-prettier@^5.5.7\",\n  