sion. BuildKit’s canonical and fallback registry tags resolve to the same manifest digest. Betterleaks 1.10.1 ships the same configuration checksum and 203-file-independent rule count as the prior patch. [Playwright release notes](https://playwright.dev/docs/release-notes) · [Buildx release](https://github.com/docker/buildx/releases/tag/v0.39.1) · [Betterleaks release](https://github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks/releases/tag/v1.10.1)\n\n## Upstream reports and retained workarounds\n\n| Report | Reproduction and downstream decision |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Browser Commander #193](https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/issues/193) | `npm ls` shows Command Stream 2.6.0 and Links Notation 0.25.2 under 0.35.0, alongside this project'\"'s newer direct dependencies. Keep upstream ranges pending the capture and config migration. |\n| [Lino i18n #45](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-i18n/issues/45) | \"'`npm ls` shows the 0.9 and 1.0 codecs installed side by side. Keep the i18n consumer'\"'s 0.9 range pending upstream roundtrip tests. |\n| [Actions Toolkit #2582](https://github.com/actions/toolkit/issues/2582) | The current SDK expects \"'`archiver.create`; Archiver 8 exports named archive classes and no longer resolves `archiver-utils` or its glob. Keep the targeted glob override until the SDK migrates. |\n| [Scrubadub #157](https://github.com/LeapBeyond/scrubadub/issues/157) | Scrubadub 2.0.1 pins TextBlob 0.15.3, whose two invalid escape sequences warn on CPython 3.14. The current TextBlob passed the same offline scanner smoke in an isolated overlay with `-W error::SyntaxWarning`. Keep the upstream-required pin in the real graph. |\n| [Existing upstream reports from PR 103](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/blob/main/dev/log/issues/102/pulls/103/upstream/reports.json) | Covers Node setup-cache ordering, Buildx failover, artifact download/ZIP behavior, the local temp cleanup adapter, Pages, Python wheels and workflow lint grammar. 