[2026-11-20T14:59:44.054Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_309","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"gh pr list --repo link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer --state merged --search 'dependency' --limit 8 --json title,number,body --jq '.[] | [.number,.title, (.body | split(\\\"\\\\n\\\") | .[0:5] | join(\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\"))] | @tsv' && gh run list --repo link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer --branch issue-223-f7aee62ca003 --limit 5 --json databaseId,conclusion,createdAt,headSha,status,name\"","aggregated_output":"103\tbuild(deps): refresh dependencies and repair upgrade regressions\tFixes #102\\\\n\\\\nThe merged Dependabot updates exposed stale workflow assertions, formatter changes and incomplete local-package lock metadata. This PR repairs those failures while preserving the upgrades, then refreshes the full npm, Deno, Python, Actions, toolchain and container dependency trees.\\\\n\\\\n- Regenerate all three npm locks and the frozen Deno graph; add a complete hash-locked Python benchmark graph. Synchronize active version pins and retain the patch Changeset for automated release.\n97\tbuild(deps): bump spacy from 3.8.16 to 3.8.18 in /experiments/benchmark in the benchmark group\tBumps the benchmark group in /experiments/benchmark with 1 update: [spacy](https://github.com/explosion/spaCy).\\\\n\\\\nUpdates `spacy` from 3.8.16 to 3.8.18\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n212\tbuild(deps): bump peter-evans/create-pull-request from 8.1.1 to 8.1.3 in the actions group\tBumps the actions group with 1 update: [peter-evans/create-pull-request](https://github.com/peter-evans/create-pull-request).\\\\n\\\\nUpdates `peter-evans/create-pull-request` from 8.1.1 to 8.1.3\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n99\tbuild(deps): bump the npm group across 2 directories with 22 updates\tBumps the npm group with 12 updates in the / directory:\\\\n\\\\n| Package | From | To |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| [@secretlint/core](https://github.com/secretlint/secretlint) | `13.0.7` | `13.1.0` |\n98\tbuild(deps): bump the actions group with 3 updates\tBumps the actions group with 3 updates: [android-actions/setup-android](https://github.com/android-actions/setup-android), [actions/cache](https://github.com/actions/cache) and [zizmorcore/zizmor-action](https://github.com/zizmorcore/zizmor-action).\\\\n\\\\nUpdates `android-actions/setup-android` from 3.2.2 to 4.0.4\\\\n<details>\\\\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n93\tfix: audit CI evidence, release integrity, and security findings\t## Problem and changes\\\\n\\\\nThe reported release passed its validation jobs, then GitHub rejected the version commit with `fatal error in commit_refs_rules`. Successful security runs also contained high-severity CodeQL findings, while runtime guards, incomplete syntax discovery, obsolete dependencies and missing evidence checks could conceal failures.\\\\n\\\\n- Retry transient push failures three times without changing the commit; keep permanent rule refusals actionable and attest release metadata against the validated parent before every push. Preserve locked dependencies during versioning, prevent post-validation source pulls, retain verified metadata-only recovery, and remove downloaded helper evaluation.\n211\tfix: decline short listed given names, end initials at their token, retry stalled installs\t## Summary\\\\n\\\\nThis PR handles all three open issues together, as #210 asks.\\\\n\\\\n- **#205:** `knownPersonal` now declines listed given names of up to three letters (`Ян`, `Ким`, `Ева`, `Ия`, `Ной`) and matches `Любви` for `Любовь`. This works next to the surname and next to the surname initial, and fake mode replaces each form as the same person.\n96\tFix preview container tooling and complete Python CI coverage\tThe main screenshot writer failed with `gh: command not found` in the pinned Playwright container ([failing run](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/actions/runs/42080626844)). Install the official GitHub CLI with a pinned checksum and run a real, read-only credential-helper smoke check in the same container on PRs before the main writer. Both event filters now cover the writer's helper dependencies.\\\\n\\\\nThe complete JavaScript/Python template comparison also identified missing Python coverage. Add pinned Ruff checks and precommit formatting, Python CodeQL, Python file-size enforcement, and a metadata-only transitive requirements audit using uv/pip-audit. Add grouped weekly Dependabot updates for every actual manifest. Keep six measured expensive test suites distributed as files are added, expand macOS Deno to six shards to eliminate the observed budget warnings without increasing timeouts, and update status-gate count assertions for the new jobs. Separate cold subprocess startup from the unchanged two-second scanner assertions in PuTTY/whitespace regression probes, reusing the established process-tree hang guard. Existing release, runtime, artifact, Pages and scanner behavior is preserved; a patch changeset prepares the next release.\\\\n\\\\n### Investigation and reproduction\n[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-20T14:59:16Z\",\"databaseId\":44758726196,\"headSha\":\"c2e7a01e05933da23f241757115fac7833c4e527\",\"name\":\"Checks and release\",\"status\":\"queued\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-20T14:59:16Z\",\"databaseId\":44758725930,\"headSha\":\"c2e7a01e05933da23f241757115fac7833c4e527\",\"name\":\"Workflows\",\"status\":\"queued\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-20T14:59:16Z\",\"databaseId\":44758725959,\"headSha\":\"c2e7a01e05933da23f241757115fac7833c4e527\",\"name\":\"Example app\",\"status\":\"queued\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-20T14:59:16Z\",\"databaseId\":44758725964,\"headSha\":\"c2e7a01e05933da23f241757115fac7833c4e527\",\"name\":\"Security\",\"status\":\"queued\"},{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-20T14:59:16Z\",\"databaseId\":4475872