[2026-11-20T15:00:09.909Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_314","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/sds-224-cache/pr-224.md <<'EOF'\nFixes #223\n\nThe merged Dependabot updates left main failing Prettier. Apply the locked formatter's output and preserve the merged dependency upgrades. The earlier npm audit failures in #212 came from a picomatch advisory that GitHub has since withdrawn. The later security run on main and the refreshed npm locks pass audit.\n\n- Regenerate all three npm locks, the frozen Deno graph and both Python hash resolutions. Update active workflow, image, scanner and release-tool pins and add Dependabot coverage for the Python resolution named in the issue.\n- Move to Command Stream 3 and Lino Objects Codec 1. The codec requires Node.js 26.13.1 or later. The major changeset records the new Node floor. Bun and Deno remain supported.\n- Use native \"'`RegExp.escape` and update regression tests to verify the Bun pin, Playwright image digest and Python audit coverage.\n- Keep the latest compatible Python 3.14 and Temurin 21 releases because the current Presidio and Capacitor toolchains constrain their newer majors. The version inventories give the reason for each retained dependency version.\n\n### Reproduction and verification\n\nRun `npx --yes prettier@3.10.1 --check docs/COVERAGE.md docs/case-studies/issue-128/research/open-source-pii.md` at main commit `5c2804c` to reproduce both formatting errors. The same command passes after the fix, and the existing CI formatting job covers both files.\n\nThree clean npm installs, three npm audits, the frozen Deno graph, Deno audit, both Python hash audits and a real spaCy model load passed locally. The existing offline benchmark completed all 224 cases, with all 210 expected spans found by the sanitizer. Focused regressions passed on Node, Bun and Deno. The app built locally and both Capacitor native projects generated successfully. The signed mobile jobs require repository configuration and run through the manual workflow. Post-merge CI on the default branch remains to be verified.\n\nThe dependency tables, baseline logs, migration sources and benchmark results are recorded with the PR. [Research and verification](https://github.com/link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer/tree/issue-223-f7aee62ca003/dev/log/issues/223/pulls/224)\n\n### Upstream reports\n\n- Command Stream and Links Notation compatibility in [Browser Commander #193](https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/issues/193)\n- Codec 1 compatibility in [Lino i18n #45](https://github.com/link-foundation/lino-i18n/issues/45)\n- Archiver 8 migration and glob deprecation in [Actions Toolkit #2582](https://github.com/actions/toolkit/issues/2582)\n- TextBlob compatibility and Python syntax warnings in [Scrubadub #157](https://github.com/LeapBeyond/scrubadub/issues/157)\nEOF\ngh pr edit 224 --repo link-foundation/sensitive-data-sanitizer --title '\"'build(deps): refresh dependencies and repair upgrade regressions' --body-file /tmp/sds-224-cache/pr-224.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
