[2026-11-20T15:04:17.866Z] [STDERR] name: Rerun unacquired jobs
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.869Z] [STDERR] # When GitHub cannot provide a hosted runner (usually macOS arm64 under
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.871Z] [STDERR] # capacity constraints) it gives up on the job with "The job was not acquired
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.872Z] [STDERR] # by Runner of type hosted even after multiple attempts". No code ran, yet the
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.873Z] [STDERR] # run is red and a push to main releases nothing. A job can also stall in its
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.875Z] [STDERR] # setup (a hung `npm ci` on one host) until a timeout ends it; when that was
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.878Z] [STDERR] # the job's `timeout-minutes`, the job and the whole run end cancelled. This
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.879Z] [STDERR] # reruns such runs, at most twice, and only when no job that ran tests failed.
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.881Z] [STDERR] # A cancelled run is rerun only when a job stalled in its setup, so a run that
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.882Z] [STDERR] # someone cancelled stays cancelled.
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.887Z] [STDERR] on:
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.889Z] [STDERR]   # Runs the default branch's code, reads only numeric run IDs from the event,
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.891Z] [STDERR]   # and never checks out the commit of the run it inspects.
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.893Z] [STDERR]   workflow_run: # zizmor: ignore[dangerous-triggers]
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.895Z] [STDERR]     workflows:
[2026-11-20T15:04:17.897Z] [STDERR]       - Checks and release
